    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
We built Atomdrift because excellent malware detection belongs to everyone — not just those who can pay for it. Open-source build pipelines get compromised too.

Atomdrift treats software like a chemist treats an unknown compound: decompose it, identify it, and reconstruct the bits that matter. ML makes the call. The math is visible. The results are reproducible.

The goal is best-of-class supply-chain detection built on contextual differential analysis. We’re not there yet — what we’re shipping today are the first building blocks.

It's all Apache-2.0. If you can't inspect how something works, it's not security. It's theater.
 </p>

